WEBVTT

00:22:59.996 --> 00:23:04.413
Do you ever have these horrible moments,
given what you study where you say,

00:23:04.913 --> 00:23:08.788
well, you know, when bad things happen,
I get good research out of it?

00:23:10.663 --> 00:23:14.079
You know, certainly during the Great
Recession, I thought that, but not now.

00:23:14.246 --> 00:23:15.454
Now I'm like, enough.

00:23:15.954 --> 00:23:18.246
Good. OK, so you're not
a bad person anymore?

00:23:18.288 --> 00:23:20.871
No, I was in graduate school
and I've reformed.

00:23:21.746 --> 00:23:25.246
Emily had a front row seat to
the dotcom fallout of 2001,

00:23:25.746 --> 00:23:28.413
and she observed similar patterns
in new graduates during

00:23:28.413 --> 00:23:30.204
the Great Recession of 2009.